Subject: [PATCH] configure: use umask 022 for config.status temp dir

The bundled configure (autoconf 2.69) creates its config.status temp
directory with `umask 077 && mktemp -d "./confXXXXXX"`. On the HarmonyOS
build filesystem (hmdfs, setgid-inherited), a mode-0700 owner temp dir is
created but subsequent writes into it are denied, producing:

  ./confXXXXXX/subs1.awk: Permission denied
  config.status: error: could not setup config files machinery

Relaxing the umask to 022 yields a mode-0755 temp dir that the owner can
write into, while still blocking group/other access. This mirrors the
established fix used elsewhere in this tree (a52dec 0002-configure-umask-022).

Patch type: portability
Upstream: not sent (environment-specific filesystem behavior)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -5317,11 +5317,11 @@
 # Create a (secure) tmp directory for tmp files.

 {
-  tmp=`(umask 077 && mktemp -d "./confXXXXXX") 2>/dev/null` &&
+  tmp=`(umask 022 && mktemp -d "./confXXXXXX") 2>/dev/null` &&
   test -d "$tmp"
 }  ||
 {
   tmp=./conf$$-$RANDOM
-  (umask 077 && mkdir "$tmp")
+  (umask 022 && mkdir "$tmp")
 } || as_fn_error $? "cannot create a temporary directory in ." "$LINENO" 5
 ac_tmp=$tmp
